.Dd October 3, 2026
.Dt JAILGRID 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jailgrid
.Nd the jailgrid web console
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm service
.Cm jailgrid
.Cm start | stop | restart | status
.Pp
.Ev JAILGRID_WEB_CONF Ns = Ns Pa web.conf
.Nm kore
.Op Fl d
.Fl c Pa kore.conf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The jailgrid console is
.Xr kore 1
with the module
.Pa jailgrid.so :
it serves the web application and its JSON API, logs its one user in
with WebAuthn, keeps the list of jail hosts, and talks to the
.Xr jailgridd 8
of each host over cblink, with mutual TLS over TCP or through a local
socket.
It runs unprivileged; everything that changes a host is done by that
host's
.Xr jailgridd 8 .
.Pp
The console shows, per host: its jails with their state and actions;
its rc.d services with their
.Xr rc.conf 5
variables; the routing table, nexthops, connections and sockets; the
packages that can be upgraded, on the host and in running jails; and
CPU, memory and ZFS usage.
Every call to a host is listed with a trace of what the host did.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Two files configure it.
.Pa kore.conf
is Kore's own: the address to bind (one
.Cm bind
line per address family), the RSA certificate for HTTPS, the user the
worker runs as, and an
.Cm include
of
.Pa routes.conf .
.Pa web.conf ,
named by the environment variable
.Ev JAILGRID_WEB_CONF ,
is the console's, in UCL:
.Bl -tag -width "update_check"
.It Va rp_id
The WebAuthn relying party: the console's host name as the browser sees
it.
Required.
.It Va origin
The exact origin the browser uses, such as
.Ql https://console.example .
Required.
.It Va rp_name
The name security keys show.
Default
.Ql Jailgrid .
.It Va datadir
Where the registered keys, the server list, the setup token and, without
.Va tls ,
the console's own certificate authority are kept; mode 0700, owned by
the worker's user.
Default
.Pa /var/db/jailgrid .
.It Va cookie_secure
Whether the session cookie is marked Secure.
Default true.
.It Va tls
A block naming certificates for
.Xr jailgridd 8
over TCP:
.Va ca ,
the authority that issued the hosts' certificates;
.Va cert
and
.Va key ,
the console's client certificate; and optionally
.Va ca_key ,
the authority's key, which lets the console enrol hosts.
Without the block the console makes an authority of its own in
.Va datadir
at first start and enrols hosts with it; see
.Xr jailgrid-enrol 8 .
.It Va update_check
False stops the console from asking the release feed for newer
versions.
Default true.
.It Va update_url
Another feed, in the shape of GitHub's
.Pa releases/latest .
.El
.Pp
The module checks every certificate it is configured with when it
loads, and refuses to start with the reason in the log; Kore serves
HTTPS only with an RSA certificate.
.Sh FIRST LOGIN
With no security key registered, the console writes a one-time token to
.Pa setup-token
in
.Va datadir
and says so in its log.
The first registration in the browser needs it; later keys are added
from a logged-in session.
A key may be a hardware key or a passkey, such as a phone's.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailgrid/kore.conf
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailgrid/web.conf
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailgrid/routes.conf
The configuration; the first two have samples next to them.
.It Pa /usr/local/lib/jailgrid/jailgrid.so
The module.
.It Pa /usr/local/www/jailgrid
The web application.
.It Pa /var/db/jailgrid
.Pa credentials.json ,
.Pa servers.json ,
.Pa setup-token ,
and with the console's own authority
.Pa ca.pem ,
.Pa ca.key ,
.Pa console.pem ,
.Pa console.key .
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/jailgrid
The
.Xr rc 8
script; variables
.Va jailgrid_enable ,
.Va jailgrid_config
and
.Va jailgrid_web_conf .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kore 1 ,
.Xr jailconf 8 ,
.Xr jailgrid-enrol 8 ,
.Xr jailgridctl 8 ,
.Xr jailgridd 8
.Pp
The API is described in
.Pa docs/openapi.yaml
of the source tree.
